From e2a17307cb2d836c27e647d922efd77737ecf69c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:22:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] estuary: the player information as one panel: the whole
 picture at a glance, the detail behind it

Key O showed about sixty small labels on its first page and no sentence that
said whether the video was playing as intended. It is now one static, opaque
panel (the picture behind it may be bright HDR, which would wash out text on
a translucent one; nothing fades or moves while it is open):

- a heading with a symbol (tick, "i" or exclamation mark, never a colour
  alone) and one sentence, decided in C++ (hades.sum.*), with what to do
  where something is not as intended, and how many other notes there are;
- the overview page: the film (what the file carries, with the badge of its
  format), Hades (what it does) and your TV (what leaves the box), a strip
  with the CPU, GPU, memory, cache and the pictures dropped and skipped, and
  the button "Change output for this video..." (PlayerControl(HadesDVOutput));
- the pages behind it, with the tabs Overview, Video, Dolby Vision, Audio and
  System (left and right): everything that the pages of Kodi and of Hades
  showed, with plainer names, nothing removed (a check compares the labels of
  the old pages with the new ones);
- the Dolby Vision page shows every level that the stream carries (L1 to L6,
  L8 to L11, L254, L255) in a table of what the file has, what Hades acts on
  and what the TV is sent, with their values;
- the Audio page draws the speakers that the layout lights;
- a value that changes while the page is open is drawn in the lighter blue
  for a moment (hades.f.*).

The strings are 32700 to 32815 of Estuary, in English and in the three
Spanish languages.
